  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HO-503001 Seeds</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project plans to refurbish and improve one or multiple community seed banks in or near  the SD=HS project sites in Uganda withthe active participation and ownership of community members. It is planned that the community seed banks will form the centre around which the activities around seed in the community will revolve including farmer field schools and adequate land for purposes of establishing demonstration plots for farmer learnings. Adequate land will also be reserved for characterization of the germplasm in the seed bank and for crop development and seed multiplication. The community seed bank will focus on all the crops that contribute tohousehold food and nutrition security, ensuring that neglected and underutilized species (NUS) that contribute to nutrition and which are important during the hunger period are given special attention. To achieve this, the main planned activities in addition to refurbishment of seed bank(s) include focus group discussions within the community, establishmentof (women led) Farmer Field Schools,food processing and preparation training sessions for NUS etc.
ONL - Team Seeds activities will take place to ensure proper monitoring and evaluation of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
